{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "770e9150-f7e2-8392-bbf4-39dd8cc6532a",
  "created_at": "2026-01-05T09:22:20-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Tito Duarte",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Greg Lombardi",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:18:58-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Greg. Good morning."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:19:02-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning. Um, I have a question about a sign? A sandwich board sign, for the sidewalk."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:19:09-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. A sandwich board, the A-frame type. What's your question on it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:19:14-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "How big can it be? Is there a size limit? I see some very big, some small, so I do not understand."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:19:23-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, there are size limits, and they're not the same everywhere in the city. It depends on where you are, downtown versus a residential street. Is this for a business?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:19:35-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, I think so? My friend has a small shop. She asks me to find out. I am just helping her."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:19:44-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. So the exact dimensions I'd want somebody to confirm for her location. But generally yes, a sandwich board on a public sidewalk needs a sign permit, and there are limits on height and width, and it can't block people walking."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:20:00-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A sign permit. Okay. So it is the sign permit, not the, um, the building permit?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:20:07-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, sign permit. Different from a building permit."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:20:11-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "And the sidewalk, is it different? The sidewalk is the city, not her shop. Is it another paper?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:20:18-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. Since it's on the public sidewalk, there can be a separate approval for that. Let me not mix it up for you. When she comes in or calls, we'll look at the exact address and tell her which pieces she needs."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:20:34-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Another question? Must a licensed contractor apply for it? Like a sign company?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:20:40-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, not for a sandwich board. The shop owner can apply herself. If a sign company is installing something permanent, like a sign bolted to the building, they'd often handle the application, but it's not required that a contractor does it for a movable board."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:20:57-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So she can apply herself. Not the contractor. Okay. And me? I can apply for her?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:21:04-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's better if she does, since she's the business. You could bring the paperwork in, though. Usually we'd want her name and signature on it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:21:14-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, her signature. I see. I thought, maybe, the one who builds the sign must sign. Now I understand a little."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:21:23-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A little's a start. [pause] Look, the easiest thing is she comes by the office with the sign's measurements and the shop address. Or you can bring those. We're open weekdays during the day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:21:36-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, measurements and address. Sorry, so the size limit, you cannot tell me today? Like a number?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:21:43-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I don't have a number I'd want to hand you over the phone, because it changes by zone. Bring the address and we'll tell you exactly."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:21:53-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. Thank you. I am also now going to her door, I bring her a casserole. She is feeling tired this week. So I will tell her all this."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:22:05-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sounds good. Tell her to bring the measurements and a photo if she has one of the board."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:22:12-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Measurements, address, photo. Yes. And she signs. Thank you very much."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:22:17-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. Have a good one."
    }
  ],
